at DISCARDS a >N-day-drifted clone's divergent local work — a destructive, irreversible operation — and states it only as an 'accepted residual' without any recovery/back-out mechanism (e.g. a backup ref or reflog snapshot before discard).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f627aac28a3aacac9","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / AC6 accepted residual","norm_id":"n9822ed5082ba295c","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A user reconnects a stale clone with unmerged local work and loses it with no recovery path"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add to the ADR's Consequences a mandated pre-override safeguard: capture the clone's local head under a dated backup ref (recoverable via reflog) before applying the remote override, so the discard is reversible in practice.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"hard","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In the ADR Decision/Consequences, cite infra/scripts/reclaim_bridge_history.py and reclaim_comment_echo_history.py and state whether the portable rewrite